WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.408
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:15.623
Unit six: My Town. Today you will describe recent changes in your town with the present perfect.

4
00:00:15.923 --> 00:00:18.540
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.942
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:25.144
Municipality.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.740
Municipality means a town or city with its own local government.

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.779
The municipality cleans the streets.

9
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:36.233
Your turn. Say: Municipality.

10
00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.521
Municipality.

11
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:42.517
Infrastructure.

12
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:47.432
Infrastructure means roads, bridges, power and water systems.

13
00:00:48.017 --> 00:00:50.655
Good infrastructure helps business grow.

14
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.042
Your turn. Say: Infrastructure.

15
00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.714
Infrastructure.

16
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:00.590
Population.

17
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:04.755
Population means the number of people living in a place.

18
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.500
The population of our town is growing.

19
00:01:08.117 --> 00:01:11.663
Your turn. Say: Population.

20
00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.606
Population.

21
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.316
Landmark.

22
00:01:18.317 --> 00:01:21.895
Landmark means a famous building or place that is easy to see.

23
00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:24.425
Wat Phnom is a famous landmark.

24
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.448
Your turn. Say: Landmark.

25
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.417
Landmark.

26
00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:33.370
Tourist attraction.

27
00:01:34.383 --> 00:01:37.730
Tourist attraction means a place that visitors love to see.

28
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:40.688
Angkor Wat is a big tourist attraction.

29
00:01:41.283 --> 00:01:44.388
Your turn. Say: Tourist attraction.

30
00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:48.629
Tourist attraction.

31
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:50.524
Local market.

32
00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:54.538
Local market means a market in your own area.

33
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.742
We buy vegetables at the local market.

34
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.165
Your turn. Say: Local market.

35
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.187
Local market.

36
00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.067
Urbanization.

37
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:11.685
Urbanization means when towns grow and more people move to cities.

38
00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:14.515
Urbanization brings new jobs.

39
00:02:15.117 --> 00:02:17.966
Your turn. Say: Urbanization.

40
00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.033
Urbanization.

41
00:02:22.783 --> 00:02:23.982
Historic site.

42
00:02:24.983 --> 00:02:28.399
Historic site means an old place that is important in history.

43
00:02:28.983 --> 00:02:32.469
Our town has a historic site from the 1920s.

44
00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:35.863
Your turn. Say: Historic site.

45
00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.142
Historic site.

46
00:02:40.883 --> 00:02:41.919
Development.

47
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:46.298
Development means growth and change, often new buildings.

48
00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:49.243
There is a lot of development near the river.

49
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.398
Your turn. Say: Development.

50
00:02:55.233 --> 00:02:56.292
Development.

51
00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:58.190
Renovation.

52
00:02:59.183 --> 00:03:02.309
Renovation means repairing an old building to make it new.

53
00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:05.183
The renovation of the market took a year.

54
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:08.598
Your turn. Say: Renovation.

55
00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:12.527
Renovation.

56
00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:14.366
Facility.

57
00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:18.325
Facility means a building or place for a special use.

58
00:03:18.917 --> 00:03:21.462
The new sports facility opened last month.

59
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.969
Your turn. Say: Facility.

60
00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:28.834
Facility.

61
00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:30.294
Growth.

62
00:03:31.283 --> 00:03:32.958
Growth means becoming bigger.

63
00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.468
Our town has seen fast growth.

64
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:38.202
Your turn. Say: Growth.

65
00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:41.731
Growth.

66
00:03:42.533 --> 00:03:46.184
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.131
Visal, has your town changed much?

68
00:03:50.217 --> 00:03:52.892
Yes! It has grown a lot recently.

69
00:03:53.983 --> 00:03:55.008
What's new?

70
00:03:56.117 --> 00:04:00.694
They have renovated the old market, and they have built a new sports facility.

71
00:04:01.783 --> 00:04:03.760
Is it a tourist attraction now?

72
00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:09.581
Yes. The historic site downtown has become very popular with visitors.

73
00:04:10.733 --> 00:04:12.466
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:16.477
Grammar focus: Present perfect plus recently.

75
00:04:16.777 --> 00:04:17.894
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:18.583 --> 00:04:20.153
The town has grown recently.

77
00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.643
They have renovated the market.

78
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.933
Recently, the population has increased.

79
00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:31.490
Use the present perfect with 'recently' or 'lately' for changes that happened not long ago.

80
00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.994
Be careful! Don't say: The town has grew recently.

81
00:04:37.933 --> 00:04:40.502
Say: The town has grown recently.

82
00:04:40.802 --> 00:04:43.626
'Grow' is irregular: grow, grew, grown.

83
00:04:44.433 --> 00:04:46.946
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:47.733 --> 00:04:49.094
A Changing Town.

85
00:04:49.394 --> 00:04:52.915
Our town's population has grown quickly due to urbanization.

86
00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.989
The municipality has improved the infrastructure, with new roads and lights.

87
00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.418
Recently, they have renovated the local market.

88
00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:06.407
A historic site downtown has become a popular tourist attraction.

89
00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:11.222
Development is good, but we must also protect our landmarks.

90
00:05:12.333 --> 00:05:15.871
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:16.717 --> 00:05:19.146
They blank renovated the market recently.

92
00:05:19.446 --> 00:05:22.728
A, have. B, has. C, are.

93
00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.266
The answer is A: have.

94
00:05:29.417 --> 00:05:32.124
The number of people living in a place is the blank.

95
00:05:32.424 --> 00:05:36.264
A, population. B, facility. C, landmark.

96
00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.741
The answer is A: population.

97
00:05:42.883 --> 00:05:45.394
Repairing an old building to make it new is blank.

98
00:05:45.694 --> 00:05:49.835
A, renovation. B, urbanization. C, growth.

99
00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.539
The answer is A: renovation.

100
00:05:56.733 --> 00:06:00.001
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:03.360
What changes have happened in your town recently?

102
00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.650
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:21.966
My town has changed a lot recently. They have built a new bridge, and a big supermarket has opened near my house.

104
00:06:22.266 --> 00:06:24.080
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:24.983 --> 00:06:29.876
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present perfect plus recently.

106
00:06:30.176 --> 00:06:34.605
Today's value is community spirit. Help and care for people in your town.

107
00:06:34.905 --> 00:06:37.279
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

108
00:06:37.579 --> 00:06:39.999
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

